/-
P3 (jc6b2, KENTRY-PLAN jc6b2): **`kernel_entry_reachU27`** = jc6d10's `kernel_entry_reachU26`
with part (b) of `RegionUnrefAt` (the bound-notification and SC–notification links, in the
`unref` halves of C16 / C22 / C24 heapH) discharged.

* P1 (jc6b2) carries the bound-link symmetry `BndS` in `ScExtra0.bs` (so in `JAtZ.blk`);
  UnrefBnd: `JAtZ.keptBW` (no bound link names a dead object, at any `JAtZ`) and
  `JAtZ.unrefBW` ((b) at an `Entered` `JAtZ` state, across the restart by `JAtZ.restartSJ`);
  `RegionUnrefCU` = (c) ∧ `DeadUnarmed`, `JAtZ.regionUnrefBCU` rebuilds U26's `RegionUnrefBCU`.
* `JUtPathMU27` / `JAsidCPathU27` / `JDevPathU27` = U26's with `unref : RegionUnrefCU`;
  `JPathMEU27` / `JPathAtMU27` / `KDispHypsKVU27` = U26's with them;
  `KDispHypsKVU27.toU26 J' hni` fills (b) from the dispatch state's own `JAtZ`.

Premise removed (relative to U26): part (b) of `RegionUnrefAt` [J] in C16, C22, C24 heapH.
Added: none in the statement; the start state's `JReachU17` (through `BlkOK`/`XInv`) now
includes P1's `BndS` (true at boot: no object bound; INV-PLAN note jc6b2). (c) and
`DeadUnarmed` unchanged. No existing statement changed.
-/
